  "editorial": "The base term is '1'. Recursively calculate the previous term, then scan each maximal equal-digit run once, appending its length and digit. Join the pieces to obtain the requested term. This directly follows the recursive definition, with depth at most 30. If L_i is the length of term i, total work is proportional to the sum of generated term lengths; working storage is O(max L_i + n), including intermediate strings and call frames. An iterative itertools.groupby implementation provides the independent oracle.",
